The plain happy path: two files, each with one frontmatter key.

`md list` prints an ABSOLUTE path in every header line, and the harness runs
each case in a scratch directory whose name is random, so the header line can
never be pinned byte for byte. Every list case that lists at least one file
therefore pipes the output through `md lines`, which selects the lines that do
not hold a path.

The plain output for this fixture is:

    1  == <scratch>/alpha.md ==
    2  title: Alpha
    3
    4  == <scratch>/beta.md ==
    5  title: Beta

so line 2 is the first file's frontmatter, serialized back to YAML.
